      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The cost argument is a major hurdle, but it ignores the massive hidden costs of our current, fragmented welfare state, which includes healthcare crises and mass incarceration driven by economic desperation. Funding UBI through progressive taxation and closing corporate loopholes is a necessary structural shift, not just an expenditure. The stability gained by eliminating systemic poverty far outweighs the fiscal adjustments required to implement a truly equitable system.",
      "source": "target",
